  "built-in-power-and-fans": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "The product page lists two AC inputs, two PSU slots and two fans; the brochure says dual redundant power supplies; the quick guide says the device takes power through two IEC C14 connectors and only one supply is active at a time, the second being for redundancy. No document held shows a removable supply module or gives a supply part number, and the rear photograph shows two bare inlets and no module handle, so the supplies are built into the chassis and there are no bays, as on juniper/ex2300-24t. The two fans are the two hexagon-grille openings of the rear photograph. The quick guide says the passive heatsinks cool the unit and the two redundant fans switch on when the ambient is above normal."
  },
  "buttons": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "One round button printed RESET (quick guide: the RouterBOOT reset button)."
  },
  "chassis": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "443 x 44 x 224 from the brochure and the product page, which agree; no drawing is held to dimension them further. 443 is the body between the ear folds. The rear heatsink is part of the depth the sources print."
  },
  "colour": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "median of photograph 1324's face (#dbdbdb)."
  },
  "console": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "The RJ45 serial port (brochure: Serial port RJ45; quick guide: RJ45 serial port, 115200 bit/s) is the upper jack of the housing, under the printed CONSOLE. The lower jack is the ETH/BOOT management Ethernet port (quick guide: Ethernet port (ETH/BOOT), can be used for network booting)."
  },
  "datasheet": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "The brochure is MikroTik's datasheet for the model: product code CRS317-1G-16S+RM, CPU 98DX8216B0 800 MHz, two cores, 1 GB RAM, 16 MB flash, 16 SFP+ cages (1.25 Gb SFP and 10 Gb SFP+, none included), 443 x 224 x 44 mm, two AC inputs of 100 - 240 V, redundant supply, 44 W maximum power consumption, -20 to 60 C tested, 38 LEDs, serial RJ45. The 44 W is unqualified in the brochure and the product page, and the quick guide words it as the consumption under maximum load, so it is filed as the maximum. The quick guide says the device was tested from -40 to +70 C; the brochure and the product page say -20 to 60 C, which is carried (the quick guide's range is a conflict declared here). The product page's suggested price is not carried."
  },
  "ears": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "Rack ears are in the box (product page, Included parts: Rack ears; the quick guide: 1U rackmount bracket, and the mounting section describes fitting them to both sides with four screws). Photograph 1324 shows them flush with the face. No drawing is held, so no distance behind the face is given. The product page also lists a K10 screw kit, which is a fastening set and not a rack kit, so no kit is listed. The ears are not drawn."
  },
  "front-layout": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - read off photograph 1324 as described under gate-1. Four blocks of four SFP+ cages, the first cage at 13.2 mm, 14.25 mm apart inside a block and 63.5 mm block to block, top at 25.8 mm. Each cage has its ACT lamp 2.55 mm and its 10G lamp 12.2 mm from its left edge, 22.4 mm down, with the legends ACT and 10G above them, and the printed SFP+ n under the cage. The CONSOLE jack (top) and the ETH/BOOT jack (below it) share one housing 17.7 mm wide at 266.0 mm; the RESET button is at 287.6 mm. The USR, FAULT, PWR 2 and PWR 1 lamps sit in a rounded bracket at 295.3 mm on a 5.1 mm pitch. The slotted vent windows over the cages and the model text are drawn as the photograph shows them."
  },
  "gate-1": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - the face of photograph 1324 is 3130 px wide between the ear folds for the printed 443 mm (7.065 px per mm) and 285 px tall for the printed 44 mm (6.48 px per mm), 0.92 of the horizontal scale, so the camera looks down and the photograph is not orthographic. Every x on the front is taken at 7.065 px per mm from the body's left edge; every y is taken at 6.48 px per mm from the face's top edge and is estimated, good to about 1 mm. The 4 x 14.25 mm SFP+ cages abut inside a block and read 100.7 px, 14.25 mm, on a quantity the scale never saw."
  },
  "lamps": {
